{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Which object slots a verb needs within arm’s reach, as opposed to merely in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view. Declared by every row of both halves of the standard table — "},{"code":"CoreVerb","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StubVerb"},{"text":" — so the answer is stated once per verb and derived from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"there.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Reach\/bothObjects","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Reach\/directObject","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Reach\/notNeeded"],"title":"Enumeration Cases","generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Reach\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/SQ","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/SH","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Reach"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parser scope is the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"visible","type":"text"}]},{"text":" set, which admits what can be seen through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"glass of a shut jar or in somebody else’s hands. Much of the table is fine"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"with that — you can smell a fire across a room, count coins behind glass,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"examine a thing you will never touch — and much of it is nonsense at a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distance, so the answer is per verb rather than a blanket guard."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three cases and not a "},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" because the two-slot shapes disagree with each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other: "},{"code":"give X to Y","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"put X in Y","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" have to reach the recipient, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"throw X at Y","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" must "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" have to reach the target, which is the whole point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of throwing. Nothing wants the indirect object alone: the two-slot verbs that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"care about the container also want the thing going into it, and a direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object already in the player’s hands passes for free."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Public because a game’s own verb has to be able to say it: a custom verb"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that carries its own default line — "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/action(_:reach:overriding:say:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"siblings — declares this column exactly as the two halves of